  "Description": {
    "Cost": 2491813,
    "UIName": "Roughneck",
    "Id": "chassisdef_roughneck_RGH-QSK-R",
    "Name": "Roughneck",
    "Details": "The Roughneck, hailing from humble beginnings as the Loader King, this Industrial mech turned Militarised workhorse has seen many a role. This specific model has come about after a former 'Notable' Solaris Arena gladiator fell on hard times. Trying to make ends meat they agreed to a sponsorship for Quicsells latest edition of their new and improved 'Quicsell Bargain battle Royale' . Packing some of the noteworthy Arena dominating Quicsell technologies does this specific version come with patented armor, a flexible TSM system and enough firepower to last a good battle. A roaring Quicsell Ultra AC 20 leads the charge backed up by their patented 'Streak' SRM launchers for accurate and conservative ammo usage. As customed to Roughneck loadouts it also brings two handheld disposable One Shot cannons for a finishing blow, then to be discarded. A small REX laser in the cockpit rounds out the armory in case of it's rather sparse ammo running out. But if the opposition isn't down by that point, it's on you soldier.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Easy to Maintain</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.07</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_roughneck"
  },
  "VariantName": "RGH-QSK-R",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "QuicsellOmni",
      "skip_hardpoint"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Quicsell gladiator",
  "YangsThoughts": "I feel pity for the poor soul that had to turn a perfectly fine machine into this excuse for a working Battlemech. Sure it's not as faultily wired or skimps on the armor as much as some of their other gimmick models. Yes there is some severe firepower here but the drawbacks, the ammo consumption is horrible on these supposed 'Premium' launchers. And the cooling, this is meant for the Arena? How badly do you want the Pilot to sweat while risking their paycheck. All considered, could have been worse but I am not betting my personal stash of Scotch on this bucket of bolts anytime soon. ",
